    "title": "Joe Mazzulla Drops Truth Bomb On Celtics‚Äô Performance After Loss To Hawks - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Daniel Fisher ,\n1 hours ago\nThe Celtics fell to the Atlanta Hawks 117-106 on Wednesday night. Following the game, head coach Joe Mazzulla offered a straightforward evaluation of Boston‚Äôs performance.\n‚ÄúJust a bad day at the office,‚Äù Mazzulla said, via WEEI‚Äôs Justin Turpin.\nThe Celtics struggled from the 3-point line, making only 9 of 34 attempts, which won‚Äôt cut it against any NBA team.\nMazzulla didn‚Äôt have his best night either, picking up a technical foul in the third quarter. He was upset that the officials missed Baylor Scheierman getting fouled, which led to Hawks forward Onyeka Okongwu grabbing the rebound and heading to the free-throw line.\n‚ÄúI think it was a little bit to get my point across, a little bit to try and spark the team and whatnot,‚Äù Mazzulla said on his technical foul, via ClutchPoints Daniel Donabedian.\nThe Celtics currently hold a 29-18 record and are clinging to the No. 2 seed in the Eastern Conference. However, they are facing increasing pressure from the New York Knicks, who also have a 29-18 record and are riding a four-game winning streak.\nMore NBA: Celtics‚Äô Sam Hauser Weighs In On Possible Jayson Tatum Return",
